<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Dorchester, Dorset</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Durnovaria</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Dorchester is the county town of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dorset">Dorset</a> in south-west <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a>. It grew from Durnovaria, the Roman town that became the administrative centre of the Durotriges, close to the great <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iron-age">Iron Age</a> hillfort of Maiden Castle. The Tolpuddle Martyrs were tried there in 1834, and the novelist Thomas Hardy, who lived nearby, portrayed it as Casterbridge.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/dorchester-dorset.jpg" alt="Dorchester, Dorset" width="320" height="315" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Alex Liivet a derivate work by MrPanyGoff · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Town_Pump_and_Corn_Exchange_-_Dorchester.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
